{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PROPOSAL — permanent fix, five surgical changes (respects all decided items: finalizer routing ADOPTED, flat forced landing WITHDRAWN, both kill paths bounded, AC-split insufficient alone):\n\n1. DETECTOR (usage_log.py): add distinct_ratio_window (window 24, trip <=0.50, order-insensitive) alongside existing metrics; compute DURING the run, not post-mortem. Fix the aec1/d166 gaps in the same change: record() default-ON (env var becomes opt-OUT), and add tool_calls to _FIELDS — the axis that separates a loop from breadth.\n\n2. ACTUATOR (new, replaces the .filtered() rewrite for landing): a detector-armed WrapperToolset. On trip, call_tool stops executing tools and returns a synthetic steering result telling the model to emit its final answer from evidence already gathered. Tools stay defined (Bedrock/Anthropic 400 proven impossible to hit), nothing raises mid-protocol, the verdict flows through the existing PromptedOutput/parse path (exp_h). Memoise the detector check once per run_step (predicate can be consulted multiple times per step).\n\n3. ESCALATION LADDER: steer for N steps (propose N=6). If the model still will not land, raise a NEW typed exception ToolLoopDetected carrying the repetition diagnostic. interpret_failure gets a typed branch AHEAD of the LLMUnavailableError sweep (else runaway = 'provider outage', the exact defect class being removed). The typed error routes CompletionAgentStep into the existing tool-free finalizer with per-criterion evidence — the ADOPTED design — instead of dying verdict-less.\n\n4. CATCH-MISS FIX (completion_recovery.py): CompletionAgentStep.run must catch LLMRunnerError-with-diagnostic (budget exhaustion) and ToolLoopDetected, not only UnretryableOutputError, so bounded recovery is actually reachable (fd84). Surface the repetition diagnostic in raise_completion_workflow_failure instead of dropping it (8b97).\n\n5. BACKSTOPS: keep request_limit AND tool_calls_limit as hard outer bounds BEHIND the steering layer (both kill paths bounded — decided). They should now only fire if steering itself fails. tool_step_limit's empty-filter rewrite must be REMOVED or replaced by steering everywhere it is armed, including completion_recovery.py:471 (_EVIDENCE_TOOL_STEPS=16) — the fallback currently carries the same 400.\n\nWHY THIS IS PERMANENT, not a seventh patch: the six prior attempts (c7c5, 7c58, b2bb, a89d, 9a08, 59bc) all adjusted BUDGETS or added REPORTING; none acted at the layer where the loop happens (the tool-call boundary) and none could land a run that had already looped. Steering acts exactly there, converts a pathological run into a verdict (the gate's entire purpose), never truncates a healthy run (detector margin 0.833 vs 0.50), and the ladder guarantees a typed, diagnosable failure instead of a masked outage when even steering fails. Budgets stop being the enforcement mechanism and become what the operator intended: failure bounds.\n\nTEST GAP TO CLOSE with the change: add a regression test asserting the request payload NEVER omits tools/toolConfig while history contains tool_use blocks (the constraint FunctionModel does not enforce) — e.g. assert the steering toolset keeps tool_defs non-empty for the whole run.\n\nOPEN FOR OPERATOR: (a) steering text + N + window/trip as config vs constants (propose constants first, config later if needed); (b) 895c (grammar-compilation 400 on plan-review) remains a SEPARATE defect — nothing here touches it. Implementation order: 70bc (detector) -> this ticket (actuator+ladder) -> fd84/8b97 fold into change 4."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785953345924359001,"uuid":"c18d1a7d-b935-4f22-a50d-863106119a0c"}